===A3_S5_D3===
Elder: You’re a wonderful storyteller, Oren, but you can’t just rewrite history, no matter what your… interpretation is. #portrait:ElderAngry
Oren: Sorry, Silas. I guess I got carried away. #portrait:Oren
Oren: Tomorrow’s story will have <i>zero</i> romantic implications, promise! …But I can’t promise the people will be happy. #portrait:Oren
Narrator: Silas sighs, hand on hip, before turning around to greet you and Chione.
Elder: When you and Amaya asked me whether Oren could host shows when you were little, I didn't expect it to become like this. #portrait:ElderAngry
Elder: Cillian is going to accuse me of favouritism at this rate. #portrait:ElderAngry
Chione: Haha… you have to admit that Oren's got talent, though. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Elder: That aside, I do have something I would like to bring up to you both. #portrait:ElderThinking
Narrator: Silas brings out an item hidden in his cloak. It's the cloth you found with Amaya!
Elder: Amaya brought this back from the human settlement earlier. They've recovered it to a readable form. #portrait:ElderThinking
Amelia: “The trees in Thavmia are not quite the kinds we are used to. But where they lack buoyancy, they are incredibly easy to work with.” #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: “We'll repurpose Starword to build the base of the ship, and find new methods to craft the deck…” #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Noelle: Is this…? #portrait:NoelleShocked
Oren: The same writing as Noah's, from other fragments we've collected over time! #portrait:Oren
Narrator: Silas lets Oren take the artifact, analysing the muddled sketches and ink left on the paper.
Oren: Bri is pretty good at copying handwriting… #portrait:Oren
Elder: Oren. #portrait:ElderAngry
Oren: Just a thought! #portrait:Oren
Amaya: I can assure you, this item is not a forgery. #portrait:AmayaThink
Narrator: Amaya's joined the party!
Narrator: She explains to you that the human settlement specialises in crafts and artifact preservation.
Amaya: If you're hoping to chase after Noah's past, they're your best bet. #portrait:
Noelle: How did you…? #portrait:AmayaThink
Narrator: Amaya shrugs, glancing at Silas. It's clear that they have the same idea.
Amaya: While nature isn't calculated, many things happen for a reason. #portrait:AmayaTalk
Amaya: And even if your connection to him isn't that deep… it's only natural for a tree to wonder where its roots hide. #portrait:AmayaThink
Elder: In return for your help these past days, we can supply you with some wood and ore for the repairing of your ship. #portrait:ElderThinking
Elder: I believe Chione has already told you about our customs regarding the floods? #portrait:ElderThinking
+[Yes, and I think…]
    -> shyerask
+[I know it may be bold of me to ask…]
    -> bolderask

===shyerask===
Noelle: I may investigate a bit more about the island and Noah, before deciding on my next moves. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
->afterchoicea3s5

===bolderask===
Narrator: Silas smiles, nodding at your silent question.
->afterchoicea3s5

===afterchoicea3s5===
Elder: We'll always welcome those who'd like to join us in the mountains. So long as they are trustworthy, and willing to help. #portrait:ElderHappy
Amelia: Well, no one else can clear ruins like you do. #portrait:AmeliaHappy
Narrator: For now, you'll probably head to the human settlement to learn more about the last flood, like Amaya suggested.
Elder: If you travel upwards through our forest you’ll arrive at the human village. #portrait:ElderThinking
Elder: They are made up of a few un-evolved bloodlines, and new faces from the last five-hundred years. #portrait:ElderThinking
Noelle: (So… Noah did contribute to a bit of sea travel amongst neighbors?) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Elder: Once you arrive, you should seek someone by the name of Cillian. He is the one responsible for all affairs — something similar to my position. #portrait:ElderThinking
Elder: There's been this one artifact that they haven't been able to unlock, due to its strange mechanisms. #portrait:ElderThinking
Elder: Perhaps if you can shed some light on that, they may be more inclined to do you a favor. #portrait:ElderHappy
Noelle: (While I might just join in Thavmia's plans, it'd still be good to fix up my boat.) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: (Our ships are more than just vehicles, after all…) #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: Thank you so much for your help. Truly. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: And to Amelia, who kindly brought me here. #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Narrator: Amelia looks away, attempting to appear nonchalant.
Amelia: Well, since you're still kind of a newcomer, I'll keep accompanying you for you. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: Looks like we're all planning to head to the mountains once the water rises, anyways. #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Amelia: Let's start getting ready for the night. Make sure you aren't leaving behind any luggage! #portrait:AmeliaHappy
-> DONE